ially boost asset prices — a key liquidity signal for', 'KEYWORDS': 'Analysis|News|BTC|FLOW', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758405910, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758405911, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422429, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52029565, 'GUID': '585684', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758405640, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/13/52029565.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin LTH Profitability Outpaces STHs: Is A New Bullish Phase About To Commence?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Semilore Faleti', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinist.com/bitcoin-lth-profitability-sth-new-bullish-phase/', 'SOURCE_ID': 13, 'BODY': 'Crypto analyst with the username PelinayPA has noted a recent shift in Bitcoin traders’ profitability with potentially strong bullish implications. Notably, the premier cryptocurrency continues to trade within the $115,000 price region after earlier price gains on Thursday were followed by a correction of equal measure. SOPR Ratio Trends Up: Market Signals Point To New Bitcoin Rally In a QuickTake post on September 19, PelinayPA shares some potential insights into Bitcoin’s future trajectory based on the latest Spent Output Profit Ratio (SOPR) developments. For context, the SOPR is an on-chain metric that reflects whether Bitcoin investors are selling their coins at a profit or a loss. However, this metric can also be used to gauge the balance of profitability between long-term holders and short-term holders when we compare the SOPR Ratios of both parties, i.e, LTH/STH SOPR. When the ratio is high (LTH > STH), it indicates that seasoned investors are more profitable, often signaling the beginning or continuation of a sustainable bull market. Conversely, when the ratio is low (LTH In the present market, the LTH/STH SOPR ratio is balanced but moving upward, a sign that long-term holders are regaining their advantage. PelinayPA suggests this could mark the early stages of a new bull cycle, with indicators pointing to $120,000 as the next major upside technical target. Bitcoin Whale Accumulation Remains High In other news, US-based institutions and whales continue to accumulate substantial levels of Bitcoin regardless of price movements. Market analyst Darkfost reports that Coinbase Premium has turned consistently positive since April, reflecting stronger institutional demand from US traders compared to entities on other trading platforms, such as Binance. At the time of writing, Bitcoin trades at $115,668 after a net 0.35% loss in the past seven days.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin|bitcoin|Bitcoin Long-Term Holders|Bitcoin Short-Term Holders|Bitcoin Spent Output Profit Ratio|BTCUSDT|CryptoQuant|Darkfost|PelinayPA', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758405763, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758405763, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 13, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinist', 'NAME': 'Bitcoinist', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/bitcoinist.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinist.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1387843200, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 48, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422401, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711620995}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52030052, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=813522', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758405600, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/52030052.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Cardano (ADA) Not Out of the Woods Yet as Analysts Expect Crash, While Mutuum Finance (MUTM) Holders Eye 44x Gains', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Cryptopolitan Media', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/cardano-ada-not-out-of-the-woods-yet-as-analysts-expect-crash-while-mutuum-finance-mutm-holders-eye-44x-gains/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'Cardano (ADA) has had a decent run, but the token could feel the bite with some rough pullback pending in 2025. Meanwhile, more and more investors are considering Mutuum Finance (MUTM) . Now available in presale for a meager $0.035, MUTM is catching the eye with its DeFi-focused lending and borrowing protocol, designed with real-world use case in mind. While ADA investors get ready for volatility, MUTM holders are watching for a potential 44x run, making it one of the hottest tokens of the next cycle. Cardano Sees Market Volatility as Investors Keep Tabs on Progress Cardano (ADA) is currently at $0.9148. The token has experienced slight movements amid widespread market fluctuation, and the performance of the price in the future hinges on network activity, technological advancement, as well as investor attitude. ADA enjoys a friendly community and regular updates, but professionals caution that it could retrace as market attitude becomes negative. In the meantime, Mutuum Finance (MUTM) is gaining attention for its innovative DeFi protocol, offering an alternative path to expansion compared to ADA. Mutuum Finance is giving investors the type of early-stage appreciation that ADA investors can never experience again. With capital seeking the next behemoth to lift off, Mutuum Finance is becoming the coin to keep an eye on. Mutuum Finance Presale FOMO Mutuum Finance provides investors the opportunity to be among the first to adopt the project and invest in tokens at much lower prices than what they will be required to pay once the project has been launched. At presale Phase 6, priced at $0.035 per MUTM, the token will be sold at Phase 7 at $0.04. Presale has been successful with over $16.01 million raised and over 16,410 token holders, a sign of positive investor sentiment and confidence in the market. As another layer of security, Mutuum Finance has introduced an official Bug Bounty Program in conjunction with CertiK that assures up to $50,000 USDT in rewards. Available to everyone, the program invites white-hat hackers, developers, and researchers to scan the codebase for any potential flaws. The rewards are tiered according to severity level, so even the low-level bugs get addressed before release. The move is just one sign of Mutuum’s commitment to investor protection, transparency, and trust. MUTM is a two-layer hybrid lending protocol, with Peer-to-Contract (P2C) and Peer-to-Peer (P2P) models, to ensure ultimate flexibility. The P2C model is used to enable the contracts to monitor the market round-the-clock so that interest rates can be decided. It is designed such that investors will earn passive income and lenders will lend at the lowest interest rates and the contracts will execute the transaction automatically. The P2P model enables direct real-time interaction between lenders and borrowers without an intermediary. The more dynamic of the two enables riskier products such as meme coins and offers freedom and efficiency in a trustless setting. For providing timely and accurate prices, Mutuum Finance utilizes Chainlink oracles that aggregate rates of high-cap tokens such as USD, ETH, MATIC, and AVAX. Fallback oracles, combined feeds, and on-chain data feeds are also utilized for providing security in a volatile market. The robust pricing foundation is utilized in stable collateral management, liquidations, and risk analysis for guaranteeing the stability and efficiency of the protocol under any condition. Mutuum Finance (MUTM) is emerging as a growth-altcoin in DeFi and Cardano (ADA) looms over market volatility. Phase 6 presale tokens cost $0.035, before rising to $0.04 in Phase 7. The project has already reached $16.01M raised and 16,410+ token holders, showcasing strong market trust. With a $50K CertiK bug bounty, a P2C/P2P lending protocol, and Chainlink-based oracle pricing, MUTM provides security, agility, and scalable DeFi infrastructure. Lock in your Stage 6 tokens today before the next presale spike. For more information regarding Mutuum Finance (MUTM) please use the following links: Website: https://mutuum.com/ Linktree: https://linktr.ee/mutuumfinance', 'KEYWORDS': 'Press Release', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758406708, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758406708, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422422, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 3, 'NAME': 'ADA', 'CATEGORY': 'ADA'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52029394, 'GUID': 'https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-up-only-mode-us-tga-850b-arthur-hayes', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758405081, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cointelegraph.png', 'TITLE': \"Crypto ready for 'up only' mode once US TGA hits $850B target: Arthur Hayes\", 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Cointelegraph by Vince Quill', 'URL': 'https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-up-only-mode-us-tga-850b-arthur-hayes?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound', 'SOURCE_ID': 16, 'BODY': 'Liquidity is set to flow into private financial markets once the United States Treasury fills its General Account with $850 billion.', 'KEYWORDS': '', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758405394, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 16, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cointelegraph', 'NAME': 'CoinTelegraph', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cointelegraph.png', 'URL': 'https://cointelegraph.com/rss', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1382227200, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 66, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422398, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711620813}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 209, 'NAME': 'DIGITAL ASSET TREASURY', 'CATEGORY': 'DIGITAL ASSET TREASURY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52029718, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=813933', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758404857, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/52029718.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Wall Street has gained $16 trillion this year despite global wars and political instability', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Jai Hamid', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/wall-streets-16-trillion-rally-powers-on/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': 'Wall Street has gained over $16 trillion in market value this year, even as the rest of the world looks like a war room. That rally has come while expected volatility in US stocks is sitting near one-year lows, and people keep throwing money at crypto, meme stocks, and anything that looks like it might pump. Oil prices are hovering near the cheapest levels seen in four years, and nobody seems to care that multiple wars are boiling around the globe. According to Bloomberg, Russia has flown drones into NATO airspace, Israel is deep into its assault on Gaza, and China keeps circling Taiwan’s coastline. Ukraine is still under siege, Japan’s government is barely standing, and France is dealing with yet another crisis. Donald Trump, back in the White House, is already swinging tariffs at everyone. He’s leading a messy trade war against allies and rivals with zero concern for who’s next. But none of that has broken the mood on Wall Street. Investors are still pouring in, eyes locked on profits instead of politics. Markets ride on earnings while ignoring bombs The general investor rule right now is this: if the geopolitical chaos doesn’t hit numbers, it doesn’t exist. That’s how Helen Jewell, chief investment officer of EMEA fundamental equities at BlackRock, framed it. “We’re very focused on geopolitical risks,” she said, “but as an investor you’ve got to look at how you can quantify that. It is the implication on consumers and currency because they are the things that impact company earnings.” So far, the impact hasn’t come. US corporate earnings are still solid. There’s no recession, and the Fed’s latest interest-rate cut has only boosted the mood. But it wouldn’t take much for that to flip. If oil prices suddenly spike, or if a major nation’s bonds collapse, the whole rally could fall apart. That’s what happened in 2022, when Russia invaded Ukraine and crude prices exploded. Wall Street dropped fast. France and Japan are also looking shaky. Their governments are weak, and their bond markets are vulnerable. That could hurt broader equity indexes if something breaks. But for now, investors are pretending those problems are far away. Guillaume Jaisson, strategist at Goldman Sachs, said flat out: “Little has been priced into stocks on geopolitical risks.” He warned that US stocks are very expensive, and Europe’s not cheap either. Political chaos already hits global stocks Trump’s policy moves are already leaving bruises. In April, he floated the highest tariffs in a century, questioned the dollar’s role as the world’s reserve currency, and triggered a selloff in Treasuries. The S&P 500 dropped nearly 20% from its high. It wasn’t just talk — investors ran for cover, and fast. Other countries haven’t been spared. The CAC 40 in France dropped over 3% in just two days after Francois Bayrou called for a vote of confidence over a budget fight. Foreign investors pulled $473 million from Indonesia’s stock market this month after violent protests and a surprise replacement of the finance minister. In Japan, investors got spooked again after Prime Minister Shigeru Ishiba announced he’d step down. These dips haven’t lasted long, though. Traders keep betting that central banks and governments will step in to stop serious damage. But Jaisson warned that if there’s a rise in uncertainty, markets could flip from treating bad news as good news to just bad news being bad. With valuations already stretched, there’s almost no room to mess up. Viktor Shvets, global strategist at Macquarie, said investors still don’t know how to react to global conflict. “Equity investors are hopeless about geopolitics; since the Vietnam War, it hasn’t had an impact,” he said. Instead of worrying about wars, they focus on things they can measure: profits, household spending, and currency movements. Still, the fallout is real. Since French President Emmanuel Macron called a snap election in June 2024, the CAC 40 has lagged behind global peers, missing out on gains fueled by AI hype and economic growth elsewhere. The FTSE 100 in the UK has also underperformed in dollar terms ever since the Brexit referendum in 2016. Now, more investors are getting nervous. A Bank of America survey showed that geopolitical risk is now rated the highest since last December in fund managers’ risk rankings. That fear is showing up in the market. A UBS basket of defense-linked stocks is up over 100% this year, and gold is hitting record highs, though that’s also because the dollar is slipping. But the real risk is still out there. Tim Murray, capital markets strategist at T. Rowe Price, warned that if these conflicts actually hit the real economy, stocks could crash hard. “A big negative economic surprise, be it politically driven or not, could mean a much bigger selloff than normal given the current valuations,” he said. KEY Difference Wire : the secret tool crypto projects use to get guaranteed media coverage', 'KEYWORDS': 'Business|Federal Reserve|USD', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758406019, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758417539, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422422, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 6, 'NAME': 'ASIA', 'CATEGORY': 'ASIA'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52028834, 'GUID': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/bitcoin-btc-supply-held-by-large-companies-revealed-here-are-the-latest-figures/', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758404047, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/52028834.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin (BTC) Supply Held by Large Companies Revealed – Here Are the Latest Figures', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Mete Demiralp', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/bitcoin-btc-supply-held-by-large-companies-revealed-here-are-the-latest-figures/', 'SOURCE_ID': 81, 'BODY': 'According to BitcoinTreasuries data, institutions hold a total of 3.74 million Bitcoins, equivalent to approximately 17.8% of the current supply. These assets are held by ETFs, public companies, governments, private companies, exchanges, and DeFi protocols. ETFs and public companies, in particular, make up the largest portion of the total. Related News: Two Whales Dumped This Altcoin: Sold in Bulk According to the data, 332 institutions currently hold Bitcoin reserves, including 192 public companies, 44 ETFs or funds, 68 private companies, 13 governments, 11 DeFi protocols, and 4 exchanges/custodians. After accounting for the ~1.1 million BTC held by Satoshi Nakamoto and the 2.3–3.7 million BTC thought to be missing, the 3.74 million BTC held by institutions equates to approximately 22.6%–24.7% of the available supply. The country with the largest Bitcoin holdings is the US (118), followed by Canada (43), the UK (21), Japan (12), and Hong Kong (12). The amount of Bitcoin held by institutions has increased significantly, particularly after the approval of cryptocurrency-holding ETFs in the US and the rise in the number of digital asset treasury companies. *This is not investment advice. Continue Reading: Bitcoin (BTC) Supply Held by Large Companies Revealed – Here Are the Latest Figures', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758404150, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758404150, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 81, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinsistemi', 'NAME': 'BitcoinSistemi', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422423, 'CREATED_ON': 1692873798, 'UPDATED_ON': 1692873836}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 6, 'NAME': 'ASIA', 'CATEGORY': 'ASIA'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 5, 'NAME': 'ALTCOIN', 'CATEGORY': 'ALTCOIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 209, 'NAME': 'DIGITAL ASSET TREASURY', 'CATEGORY': 'DIGITAL ASSET TREASURY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52028714, 'GUID': 'https://timestabloid.com/?p=83815', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758403831, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Copy Trading in Crypto – How Beginners Can Profit Like the Pros', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'PR Desk', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/copy-trading-in-crypto-how-beginners-can-profit-like-the-pros/', 'SOURCE_ID': 67, 'BODY': 'The fast-paced world of cryptocurrency trading can mean that charts change dramatically from one minute to the next, and news items that ignite a “fear of missing out” among ordinary investors one day can send prices plunging the other way overnight. For a lot of newer players, this progress seems absolutely impossible to achieve. Which is why copy trading has become so big: It lets beginners mimic the orders of professional traders, allowing them to benefit from and even learn from their expertise without having to spend years honing it. For beginners, copy trading is changing the game in how consumers participate in the market, but it’s not the only path to potential growth. For presale options, demand is also skyrocketing. And through them, MAGACOIN FINANCE has stood out most and attracted whales as well as early retail investors. Understanding the Appeal of Copy Trading The fast-paced world of cryptocurrency trading can mean that charts change dramatically from one minute to the next, and news items that ignite a “fear of missing out” among ordinary investors one day can send prices plunging the other way overnight. For a lot of newer players, this progress seems absolutely impossible to achieve. Which is why copy trading has become so big: It lets beginners mimic the orders of professional traders, allowing them to benefit from and even learn from their expertise without having to spend years honing it. For beginners, copy trading is changing the game in how consumers participate in the market, but it’s not the only path to potential growth. For presale options, demand is also skyrocketing. And through them, MAGACOIN FINANCE has stood out most and attracted whales as well as early retail investors. At its most basic level, copy trading is simple. An investor chooses a trader whose trading record they’d like to mimic publicly, connects their account through a copy trading platform and their account will then automatically replicate all the trades of that professional. If the trader is buying Bitcoin, the investor’s account buys Bitcoin. The trader gets profits, and so does the investor. This configuration allows those new to the market the opportunity to take advantage of professional strategies without learning technical analysis overnight. That is particularly true in crypto, where volatility breeds caution even among the most experienced traders. Beginners can have more confidence in assuming trades that they’d otherwise shy away from by replicating someone who already has experience. Benefits That Attract Newcomers One of the most significant advantages of copy trading is that it allows learning through participation. Watching trades unfold in real time helps beginners understand why certain moves are made, what patterns traders look for, and how risk is managed. Over time, this exposure can help newcomers develop their own style. Another benefit is time. Many beginners don’t have the hours each day to study charts, read research, or track every news update. Copy trading lets them participate in the market passively while still learning on the side. There’s also the potential to generate consistent results if the chosen trader has a reliable record. While there are no guarantees, aligning with a skilled strategist gives beginners a better chance than guessing on their own. The Risks That Must Be Managed Despite the appeal, copy trading carries real risks. The most obvious is over-reliance. Just because a trader has performed well in the past doesn’t mean they will continue to do so indefinitely. Market conditions change, and even professionals face drawdowns. There are also platform fees, performance charges, and the issue of slippage—when large numbers of people copy the same trader, execution prices can differ. This means returns may not precisely match those of the lead trader. Finally, beginners may find themselves copying strategies that involve risk levels far beyond their comfort zone. Some traders thrive on high leverage, which can lead to big wins but also wipeouts. Without caution, following the wrong profile can cause losses just as quickly as gains. An Alternative for Beginners While many newcomers are exploring copy trading, others are turning their attention to early presales as an alternative route into the market. MAGACOIN FINANCE is one of the names dominating the discussion. Forecasts suggest it could deliver up to 22,000% ROI by 2025, putting it in the spotlight as a potential breakout candidate for the next bull cycle. The presale is attracting both whale inflows and retail demand, with investors eager to secure allocations before wider listings. Adding to the urgency, early buyers can unlock a 50% EXTRA BONUS with the code PATRIOT50X, effectively boosting their positions. With phases selling out quickly, this presale highlights the other side of beginner strategy—where instead of copying someone else’s trades, investors position themselves early in projects with high growth potential. How To Use Copy Trading Wisely For those who do choose copy trading, discipline is essential. Beginners should avoid putting all their capital into a single trader. Spreading allocations across several different profiles reduces the risk of one poor performance wiping out an account. Monitoring results regularly is also essential. If a trader suddenly changes strategies or starts chasing risky bets, it may be time to reduce exposure. Having personal stop-loss settings in place adds another layer of control, ensuring losses don’t spiral out of hand. Ultimately, copy trading works best as part of a broader strategy. Beginners can combine it with long-term holdings in established assets, small positions in promising presales, and gradual self-education. Over time, many investors evolve from pure copy trading into building their own independent strategies. Conclusion Copy trading has given beginners a way to step into crypto without feeling overwhelmed, offering the chance to profit while learning from experienced traders. But like any tool, it comes with risks that require careful management. Presale opportunities such as MAGACOIN FINANCE provide another powerful option, letting investors capture upside by entering early before the broader market catches on. For new participants in crypto, the key is balance: combining education, security, and disciplined allocation to find a strategy that fits both goals and risk tolerance. To learn more about MAGACOIN FINANCE, visit: Website: https://magacoinfinance.com Access: https://magacoinfinance.com/access Twitter/X: https://x.com/magacoinfinance Telegram: https://t.me/magacoinfinance Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Times Tabloid, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice. Times Tabloid is not responsible for any financial losses. The post Copy Trading in Crypto – How Beginners Can Profit Like the Pros appeared first on Times Tabloid .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Finance|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758403914, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 67, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'timestabloid', 'NAME': 'TimesTabloid', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422416, 'CREATED_ON': 1664381507, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673235440}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 47, 'NAME': 'SPONSORED', 'CATEGORY': 'SPONSORED'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52028409, 'GUID': 'https://news.bitcoin.com/?p=757651', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758403259, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/14/52028409.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Ethereum Liquid Staking Shake-Up: $268M Outflow Hits LSPs', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Jamie Redman', 'URL': 'https://news.bitcoin.com/ethereum-liquid-staking-shake-up-268m-outflow-hits-lsps/', 'SOURCE_ID': 14, 'BODY': 'While ethereum-liquid staking protocols (LSPs) welcomed a hefty 690,000 ETH influx across 14 weeks until the end of August, the tide has since shifted, with LSPs watching 60,000 ETH slip away in just the last 27 days. Billions in Motion: Ethereum Liquid Staking Now Worth $63.99B ETH LSPs have shed $268.55 million — about 60,000', 'KEYWORDS': 'Defi|Ethereum (ETH)|Liquid Staking', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758403329, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758403330, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 14, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoin.com', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin.com', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/bitcoincom.png', 'URL': 'https://news.bitcoin.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1438387200, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 51, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422399, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711621233}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 24, 'NAME': 'ETH', 'CATEGORY': 'ETH'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52028076, 'GUID': 'https://en.coinotag.com/chainlink-could-see-potential-breakout-to-125-amid-link-accumulation-saudi-awwal-bank-partnership-and-low-exchange-reserves/', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758402490, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/52028076.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Chainlink Could See Potential Breakout to $125 Amid LINK Accumulation, Saudi Awwal Bank Partnership and Low Exchange Reserves', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Crypto Vira', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/chainlink-could-see-potential-breakout-to-125-amid-link-accumulation-saudi-awwal-bank-partnership-and-low-exchange-reserves/', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': 'Chainlink price prediction for September: Major partnerships, falling exchange reserves and institutional accumulation point to a bullish outlook. Short-term resistance is near $25.8, with potential longer-term targets at $31, $38', 'KEYWORDS': 'News|LINK', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758402555, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758402556, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422429, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 31, 'NAME': 'LINK', 'CATEGORY': 'LINK'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52027979, 'GUID': 'https://cryptopotato.com/?p=413079', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758402394, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/27/52027979.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'CZ Warns Crypto Firms of North Korean Hacker Threats', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Wayne Jones', 'URL': 'https://cryptopotato.com/cz-warns-crypto-firms-of-north-korean-hacker-threats/', 'SOURCE_ID': 27, 'BODY': 'Binance founder Changpeng Zhao (CZ) has issued a warning to crypto projects about North Korean hackers. He detailed how the group is using increasingly sophisticated tactics to gain access to companies. Operatives Are Exploiting Hiring Process CZ shared his concerns via a September 18 X post, describing the hackers as “advanced, creative, and patient.” He explained how the most common method used by these individuals involves posing as job candidates to secure roles in companies, particularly in developer, security, and finance positions, giving them a “foot in the door.” In other cases, the group poses as employers and attempts to interview staff, using the process to distribute malware. Zhao noted that during these sessions, the attackers often claim there is a problem with Zoom and then send a link to an “update” carrying a virus, or they provide coding questions followed by “sample code” embedded with malware. Another tactic involves pretending to be users who file customer support requests containing malicious links. CZ added that hackers also pay or bribe employees and hired vendors to gain access to data, pointing to a recent case in India where an outsourcing service was compromised, resulting in the leak of data from a major U.S. exchange and losses exceeding $400 million. This alert follows the release of a report by cybersecurity group Security Alliance (SEAL), profiling over 60 impostors linked to North Korean operations. The report says that these attackers built fake LinkedIn profiles, set up GitHub portfolios, and used forged government IDs to make their applications look real. Shift in Methods North Korean hackers have always been a major threat in the crypto industry, with over $1.3 billion worth of assets stolen in 2024 alone. Traditionally, they have relied on phishing, malware, and private key compromises to loot from exchanges. However, recent reports suggest they are moving towards targeting human resources. A separate investigation by ZachXBT also uncovered how a small DPRK team of five IT workers operated over 30 fake identities at crypto firms. Elsewhere, Coinbase also recently reported a similar threat from these bad actors. The exchange shared that they are increasingly targeting their remote worker policy to infiltrate sensitive systems. CEO Brian Armstrong has since announced changes to the company’s internal security protocols, including mandatory in-person onboarding in the U.S., fingerprinting, and U.S. citizenship requirements for employees with system-level access. The exchange also introduced stricter interview procedures, such as requiring cameras to remain on, to prevent impersonation and AI-assisted coaching. In light of the growing threat to the job market, CZ has urged crypto platforms to train their employees not to download files and to screen potential candidates carefully. The post CZ Warns Crypto Firms of North Korean Hacker Threats appeared first on CryptoPotato .', 'KEYWORDS': 'AA News|Crypto News|Changpeng Zhao (CZ Binance)|Hacks|Lazarus Group|North Korea', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758402413, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758402413, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 27, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopotato', 'NAME': 'Crypto Potato', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopotato.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptopotato.com/category/crypto-news/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1458086400, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 57, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422399, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711621041}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 74, 'NAME': 'BNB', 'CATEGORY': 'BNB'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52027853, 'GUID': 'https://ambcrypto.com/?p=530173', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758402002, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'TITLE': 'Can Chainlink’s tie up with Saudi Awwal Bank propel LINK to $125?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Akashnath S', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/can-chainlinks-tie-up-with-saudi-awwal-bank-propel-link-to-125/', 'SOURCE_ID': 32, 'BODY': 'The cup and handle pattern spotted on the higher timeframe price charts signaled a possible bullish breakout to $125.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Altcoin|ChainLink|News|News 1|No Homepage|Social|Trading View|ambcrypto', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758402097, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 32, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'ambcrypto', 'NAME': 'AMB Crypto', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422425, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1674467937}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 31, 'NAME': 'LINK', 'CATEGORY': 'LINK'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 5, 'NAME': 'ALTCOIN', 'CATEGORY': 'ALTCOIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52028612, 'GUID': 'https://invezz.com/?p=2891158', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758402000, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/69/default.png', 'TITLE': 'MAGACOIN FINANCE surpasses $14M presale as ADA, LINK investors pile in', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Collaborations', 'URL': 'https://invezz.com/news/2025/09/20/magacoin-finance-surpasses-14m-presale-as-ada-link-investors-pile-in/', 'SOURCE_ID': 69, 'BODY': 'MAGACOIN FINANCE has passed the $14 million mark in its presale, gaining traction in the crypto market. What is notable in this rush is the kind of capital that is coming in. Investors with blue-chip assets in their portfolios, such as Cardano (ADA) and Chainlink (LINK), are now pouring money into this new token. The acquisition is an indicator of a changing approach since whales and industry veterans are combining proven projects with new ventures, with more probable upward progress. This is a relevant trend that indicates an increased awareness of the continuously changing market in 2025. ADA and LINK remain large-cap assets that have merged reliability and technological leadership, but their big valuations inherently slow down the exponential growth of their prices. Conversely, presales such as MAGACOIN FINANCE offer the chance to buy at lower prices and wait for exponential gains when liquidity and exchange listings happen. The appeal lies in timing, risk-versus-reward, and the potential for outsized gains that established assets can no longer deliver. Established giants: Cardano and Chainlink hold their ground Cardano is among the most well-known sources of smart contracts, with support for sustainability and security. Their proof-of-stake design has placed it among energy efficiency leaders, and its scaling solutions, named Hydra and rising DeFi partnerships, are expanding its usefulness. To its persistent supporters, ADA stands as a home for technological progress and usage. However, its maturity curbs the hyper-growth that it experienced in earlier years, which then makes some holders venture into more speculative players. On the other hand, Chainlink controls the decentralized oracle space. It has linked blockchains to real-world data, making it essential to decentralized finance, gaming, and Enterprise adoption. New alliances in tokenized assets and integrations on a broader scale shed more light on the continued relevance of LINK. Nonetheless, its billion-dollar market capitalization has ensured that its growth curve is more incremental than exponential. This fact has prompted investors to look beyond its gradual trend to the newer tokens that may repeat the initial success of earlier cycles. The appeal of MAGACOIN FINANCE’s presale MAGACOIN FINANCE positions itself as a high-upside, low-cap opportunity that contrasts sharply with the size and stability of ADA and LINK. In presale, investors acquire tokens at entry points designed to reward early adoption. These discounted levels, combined with scarcity-focused tokenomics, give buyers a chance to benefit from appreciation once listings and liquidity expand. The project’s roadmap also plays into its appeal. With planned features in decentralized finance and community governance, MAGACOIN FINANCE seeks to carve out a distinct niche. Whales have taken note of this structure, seeing it as an opportunity to complement their blue-chip holdings with a token that carries higher potential return. The more than $14 million raised so far underscores this confidence. Portfolio diversification in 2025 The influx of ADA and LINK investors into MAGACOIN FINANCE indicates a bigger tendency among portfolio tactics. Blue-chip cryptos are stable, whereas presales generate momentum and new growth opportunities. The combination of the two will form a balanced strategy that is consistent with the realities of the present market. Investors are no longer deciding between safety and opportunity, but rather merging them to ensure optimization. This diversification plan indicates the extent to which the market has evolved. Earlier cycles had concentrated much of the capital on Bitcoin, Ethereum, and a few other leading projects. Capital allocation today is increasingly dynamic with institutional adoption, real-world asset tokenization, and the rapid emergence of new platforms. The presale success experienced by MAGACOIN FINANCE underscores the fact that established investors are also prepared to commit to a start-up project when growth opportunities outweigh risks. Conclusion The presale milestone reached by MAGACOIN FINANCE demonstrates the evolving strategies shaping crypto portfolios in 2025. Cardano and Chainlink remain indispensable to the blockchain ecosystem, but their growth curves are steady rather than explosive. By contrast, MAGACOIN FINANCE offers investors an early-entry advantage that may translate into higher returns once listings and liquidity arrive. For whales and retail backers alike, this balance between proven networks and presale opportunities is becoming a defining feature of the next phase in crypto investing. To learn more about MAGACOIN FINANCE, visit: Website: https://magacoinfinance.com Access: https://magacoinfinance.com/access Twitter/X: https://x.com/magacoinfinance Telegram: https://t.me/magacoinfinance . The post MAGACOIN FINANCE surpasses $14M presale as ADA, LINK investors pile in appeared first on Invezz', 'KEYWORDS': 'Crypto|Sponsored', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758403700, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 69, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'invezz', 'NAME': 'Invezz', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/69/default.png', 'URL': 'https://invezz.com/news/cryptocurrency/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422421, 'CREATED_ON': 1679069939, 'UPDATED_ON': 1679076581}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 3, 'NAME': 'ADA', 'CATEGORY': 'ADA'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 31, 'NAME': 'LINK', 'CATEGORY': 'LINK'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52029226, 'GUID': '252fc13d-7e33-4313-93a7-88e8f2ba6350', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758402000, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/5/52029226.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Internet Computer Bets Big on AI as Crypto Markets Play Catch-Up', 'SUBTITLE': 'This could be the beginning of a new tech stack — one in which AI, not humans, becomes the primary developer of applications, says Dfinity founder Dominic Williams.', 'AUTHORS': 'Jamie Crawley,AI Boost', 'URL': 'https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2025/09/20/internet-computer-bets-big-on-ai-as-crypto-markets-play-catch-up', 'SOURCE_ID': 5, 'BODY': 'The Internet Computer (ICP), a blockchain project that has sought to differentiate itself from rivals, is doubling down on its pitch as the go-to network for on-chain artificial intelligence (AI). This could be the beginning of a new tech stack - one in which AI, not humans, becomes the primary developer of applications, according to Dominic Williams, founder of Internet Computer developer Dfinity. Williams argued that while crypto prices remain driven largely by market mechanics - treasury operations, liquidity games and speculation - the underlying technology will eventually force a reckoning in an interview with CoinDesk. “In the long run, markets begin to reflect realities on the ground,” he said. “But as yet you’re not seeing what’s happening with Internet Computer reflected in ICP’s price.” Running AI on-Chain The Internet Computer first demonstrated neural networks running as smart contracts in April last year, starting with image classification and later facial recognition, Williams said. While those were relatively simple models compared to large language models - the kind that power AI tools like ChatGPT and Gemini - they were proof of concept: that AI can run natively on a blockchain. No other network has achieved this, Williams pointed out, despite the chatter about “decentralized AI.” Where others rely on off-chain infrastructure like Amazon Web Services, ICP seeks to integrate the full AI development and execution stack on-chain. Williams describes this as “a self-writing internet” - a system where users describe what they want, and an AI delivers it as a working application, hosted directly on Internet Computer. The bigger idea, Williams said, is that AI itself will replace much of today’s developer workflow. Instead of humans writing code, configuring databases and maintaining servers, an AI could spin up applications instantly, update them continuously and ensure resilience through blockchain-based guarantees. This reframes the blockchain not just as a settlement layer for tokens, but as the optimal environment for AI-generated applications. ICP’s design, with features like “reverse gas” - the model where developers pay for the computational costs of their applications, rather than requiring end users to pay a transaction fee - removes the need for firewalls or database migrations that plague traditional infrastructure. “AI is developing these apps hundreds of times faster than humans could,” Williams said. “And because there are no system admins standing by, you need the guardrails only blockchain can provide.” Williams pointed to early hackathons where ordinary people used AI on ICP to build apps: from a crowdsourced pothole-mapping platform, to a tool for generating wills and health directives. The vision is that such tools could proliferate in the millions. Entrepreneurs, small businesses and even NGOs could create customized apps without technical expertise, paying for usage with fiat while crypto tokens underpin the system behind the scenes. Price Action Still Lagging Despite these developments, the ICP token has yet to see sustained momentum. It briefly rallied when AI integrations were announced last year, but has since traded more in line with broader market sentiment than with user adoption. Williams accepts this disconnect but predicts that markets may catch up very soon. “This could be the first time Web3 actually outcompetes Web2 technologically, without a token incentive in sight,” Williams said. “The shock will be when people realize they can just talk to an AI, and a blockchain app appears at a URL.”', 'KEYWORDS': 'Tech|Internet Computer|AI|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758405044, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758405044, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 5, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coindesk', 'NAME': 'CoinDesk', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/5/default.png', 'URL': 'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/?outputType=xml', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1367884800, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 71, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422397, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1744296800}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 82, 'NAME': 'ICP', 'CATEGORY': 'ICP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52027810, 'GUID': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/?p=824852', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758402000, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/21/52027810.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Shiba Inu Joins The Ranks Of Dogecoin, XRP On Coinbase ETF Watchlist – The Next Big Thing?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Scott Matherson', 'URL': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/altcoin/shiba-inu-joins-the-ranks-of-dogecoin-xrp-on-coinbase-etf-watchlist-the-next-big-thing/', 'SOURCE_ID': 21, 'BODY': 'Shiba Inu is now entering the same space as some of the largest cryptocurrencies when it comes to discussing exchange-traded funds (ETFs). The SHIB coin is starting to gain notice as it appears on Coinbase’s radar. Coinbase already offers a futures product for Shiba Inu, and this step positions the meme coin for consideration as a future ETF. SHIB’s marketing lead claims the coin already has the necessary setup for this, while a market analyst predicts significant price growth. Both agree that momentum for SHIB is picking up now. Related Reading: From $2 Trillion To $400T? CEO Sees Bitcoin Exploding 200x – Here’s More Shiba Inu Enters Coinbase’s ETF Watchlist According to SHIB’s marketing lead, Susie S, the coin has now joined Coinbase’s “ETF Watchlist Club.” This group already includes Dogecoin (DOGE), Solana (SOL), Hedera (HBAR), and XRP. Being named in this group indicates that the Shiba Inu token is gaining more serious attention. Susie S explained that Shiba Inu is in line for spot ETF consideration because Coinbase already has a regulated futures contract called the “1K SHIB Index.” It is essential because it puts SHIB on the same pathway that Bitcoin (BTC) and Ethereum (ETH) followed before they gained approval for spot ETFs. For the first time, the meme coin now stands in the same conversation as two of the world’s largest cryptocurrencies. She added that while it may be harder for Shiba Inu to launch its own solo ETF immediately, the ETF could be part of a larger product. That product could be something like a “Top 10 Crypto ETF” that bundles together several coins. Market Analyst Sees Massive Potential For SHIB Price Market analyst Heber Mayen also sees a big future for Shiba Inu. Posting a SHIB price chart on X, he stated, “It’s gonna be massive!” His comment reflects the rising attention around Shiba Inu as it becomes more active in trading markets. Mayen explained that SHIB’s popularity on Coinbase’s perpetual markets is a significant indicator. As more traders buy and sell SHIB in these products, the trading volume goes up. This rise in volume can help SHIB meet one of the needs for an ETF to be approved. In other words, the more people trade Shiba Inu now, the stronger the case becomes for a future ETF. Related Reading: FalconX Moves 413K Solana Worth $98M – Impact On SOL Price Currently, Shiba Inu is attracting more leveraged traders, and this ETF activity may be fueling ongoing speculation. Analysts like Mayen argue that momentum is on SHIB’s side as investors seek the next big crypto ETF candidate. The price action and volume activity together create the type of market story that can push Shiba Inu further into the spotlight. Backed by comments from its marketing lead and bullish words from the analyst, the SHIB meme coin could become the next big thing. Featured image from Unsplash, chart from TradingView', 'KEYWORDS': 'Altcoin|altcoins|blockchain|coinbase|crypto|crypto market|crypto news|cryptocurrency|Dogecoin|Shiba Inu|xrp', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758402071, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758402071, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 21, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'newsbtc', 'NAME': 'NewsBTC', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/newsbtc.png', 'URL': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1380585600, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 50, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422399, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711620962}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 44, 'NAME': 'SHIB', 'CATEGORY': 'SHIB'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 20, 'NAME': 'DOGE', 'CATEGORY': 'DOGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52027559, 'GUID': 'https://decrypt.co/?p=340511', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758401343, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/44/52027559.jpeg', 'TITLE': \"Americans Want AI's Benefits But Fear Losing What Makes Them Human: Survey\", 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Jose Antonio Lanz', 'URL': 'https://decrypt.co/340511/americans-want-ai-benefits-fear-losing-makes-human', 'SOURCE_ID': 44, 'BODY': 'A new Pew Research survey reveals deepening anxiety about AI, with the majority of American respondents believing it will erode creativity and relationships.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758401511, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758401511, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 44, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'decrypt', 'NAME': 'Decrypt', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/decrypt.png', 'URL': 'https://decrypt.co/feed', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1521331200, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 57, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422410, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711620560}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 64, 'NAME': 'RESEARCH', 'CATEGORY': 'RESEARCH'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026915, 'GUID': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/xrp-liquidation-imbalance-analyst-explains-what-it-means/', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758400088, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/52026915.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'XRP Liquidation Imbalance: Analyst Explains What It Means', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Mete Demiralp', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/xrp-liquidation-imbalance-analyst-explains-what-it-means/', 'SOURCE_ID': 81, 'BODY': 'Ripple (XRP) experienced sharp volatility in the cryptocurrency market over the last 24 hours. According to CoinGlass data, a total of $7.93 million worth of XRP positions were liquidated. $7.21 million of this came from long positions and $718,000 from short positions. This brought the daily liquidation imbalance to a record 903%. The XRP price fell from $3.04 to $2.98 during the day, falling below the critical $3 psychological support level. While the $2.90 level is currently being held as support, the market is showing no signs of a strong recovery. The sharp decline was not limited to XRP alone. On the Ethereum (ETH) side, a total of $61.5 million worth of long positions were liquidated, while short losses were limited to $4.14 million. A similar picture was seen for Bitcoin (BTC): $35.1 million was liquidated, $33.1 million of which came from long positions. The higher liquidation rate for long positions compared to short positions may indicate a weakening of buyer appetite in the market. Some analysts suggest that the decline may be due to strategic price pressure from institutional investors rather than a simple correction. Black Swan Capitalist founder Versan Aljarrah and financial writer Jim Willie argue that institutions are holding back the rally to accumulate XRP at its low price. “If it weren’t for these pressures, XRP could have risen to at least $7-$8 from its recent price movements,” Willie said, adding that institutions see XRP as a liquidity tool instead of the US dollar and take long-term positions. *This is not investment advice. Continue Reading: XRP Liquidation Imbalance: Analyst Explains What It Means', 'KEYWORDS': 'News|XRP', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEGATIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758400146, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758400147, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 81, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinsistemi', 'NAME': 'BitcoinSistemi', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422423, 'CREATED_ON': 1692873798, 'UPDATED_ON': 1692873836}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026721, 'GUID': 'https://news.bitcoin.com/?p=757569', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758399603, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/14/52026721.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'GENIUS Act Plumbing: US Treasury Seeks Public Input on Stablecoin Guardrails', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Jamie Redman', 'URL': 'https://news.bitcoin.com/genius-act-plumbing-us-treasury-seeks-public-input-on-stablecoin-guardrails/', 'SOURCE_ID': 14, 'BODY': 'The U.S. Treasury Department is officially opening the floor for public comment on how to implement the nation’s first major stablecoin law. Treasury Invites Comment on Stablecoin Oversight The Advance Notice of Proposed Rulemaking (ANPRM) asks the public to weigh in on how the Treasury should tailor safeguards for payment stablecoins without choking off innovation.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Regulation|Stablecoin|US Treasury', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758399776, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758399777, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 14, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoin.com', 'NAME': 'Bitcoin.com', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/bitcoincom.png', 'URL': 'https://news.bitcoin.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1438387200, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 51, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422399, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711621233}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 210, 'NAME': 'MACROECONOMICS', 'CATEGORY': 'MACROECONOMICS'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026582, 'GUID': 'https://en.coinotag.com/bitcoin-could-gain-price-and-adoption-as-fourth-turning-style-reset-erodes-trust-in-institutions/', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758399331, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/52026582.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin Could Gain Price and Adoption as Fourth Turning-Style Reset Erodes Trust in Institutions', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Jocelyn Blake', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/bitcoin-could-gain-price-and-adoption-as-fourth-turning-style-reset-erodes-trust-in-institutions/', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': 'Bitcoin adoption is accelerating as declining trust in institutions, rising government debt and worsening consumer confidence push individuals toward a neutral, permissionless store of value; Bitcoin price and adoption are', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin|News|BTC|FLOW', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758399438, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758399438, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422429, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 125, 'NAME': 'FLOW', 'CATEGORY': 'FLOW'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026429, 'GUID': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/bnb-breaks-another-record-heres-the-estimated-wealth-of-cz-after-the-latest-surge/', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758399069, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/52026429.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'BNB Breaks Another Record! Here’s the Estimated Wealth of CZ After the Latest Surge', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Mete Demiralp', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/bnb-breaks-another-record-heres-the-estimated-wealth-of-cz-after-the-latest-surge/', 'SOURCE_ID': 81, 'BODY': \"A remarkable development has occurred in the cryptocurrency market. According to 8market data, the market value of Binance's native coin, BNB, has reached $141.79 billion. This figure moved BNB to 155th place in the global asset market capitalization rankings, surpassing Intel with a market capitalization of $138.14 billion. According to a June 2024 report by Forbes, Binance founder Changpeng Zhao (CZ) held approximately 89.1 million BNB at the time. The recent surge in the BNB price, reaching over $1,020, has brought the value of CZ's holdings to approximately $90.88 billion. Related News: Has the Altcoin Season Begun? Here's the Latest Status According to the Index CZ's other known crypto asset portfolio is as follows: SHORT: 3.996 trillion units ($115.68 million) BNB: 958,841 units ($979.33 thousand) SIREN: 1.775 million units ($173.56 thousand) QUQ: 84.934 million units ($144.58 thousand) JANITOR: 50 million units ($80.76 thousand) However, of the cryptocurrencies listed above, only BNB is an asset Zhao willingly owns. The others are memecoins sent by developers to draw attention to CZ. Reliable data on the total supply of SHORT, which holds the largest share, is lacking, and caution is warranted. *This is not investment advice. Continue Reading: BNB Breaks Another Record! Here’s the Estimated Wealth of CZ After the Latest Surge\", 'KEYWORDS': 'Binance Coin|News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758399097, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758399097, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 81, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinsistemi', 'NAME': 'BitcoinSistemi', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422423, 'CREATED_ON': 1692873798, 'UPDATED_ON': 1692873836}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 74, 'NAME': 'BNB', 'CATEGORY': 'BNB'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 5, 'NAME': 'ALTCOIN', 'CATEGORY': 'ALTCOIN'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026321, 'GUID': 'https://en.coinotag.com/bitcoin-could-extend-september-gains-after-holding-116k-support-as-nvm-reset-and-long-bias-signal-123k-130k-potential/', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758398792, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/52026321.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin Could Extend September Gains After Holding $116K Support as NVM Reset and Long Bias Signal $123K–$130K Potential', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Crypto Vira', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/bitcoin-could-extend-september-gains-after-holding-116k-support-as-nvm-reset-and-long-bias-signal-123k-130k-potential/', 'SOURCE_ID': 77, 'BODY': 'Bitcoin’s September 2025 performance shows resilience: BTC climbed ~8%, held the $116K–$117K trendline support, and saw declining exchange reserves plus rising leveraged longs, suggesting momentum toward the $122K–$123K resistance and', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin|News|BTC|FLOW', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758398873, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758398873, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 77, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'coinotag', 'NAME': 'CoinOtag', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/77/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.coinotag.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422429, 'CREATED_ON': 1686819961, 'UPDATED_ON': 1717748924}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 125, 'NAME': 'FLOW', 'CATEGORY': 'FLOW'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026254, 'GUID': 'https://timestabloid.com/?p=83874', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758398757, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'TITLE': 'Journalist: All Evidence Points to XRP and XRPL Being Used After the Laws Are Effective', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Zaccheaus Ogunjobi', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/journalist-all-evidence-points-to-xrp-and-xrpl-being-used-after-the-laws-are-effective/', 'SOURCE_ID': 67, 'BODY': 'The next chapter of cross-border payments is quietly unfolding, setting the stage for programmable ledgers and audited stablecoins to move from theory to mainstream practice. As regulatory barriers fall , the focus is shifting away from speculation and toward the infrastructure that can settle value across borders with near-instant finality. Journalist Vincent Scott recently highlighted a crucial milestone on X, emphasizing that the XRP Ledger’s true potential will be unlocked and adoption will accelerate once clear regulations are established. His comments reflect a broader consensus among analysts and market observers: regulatory clarity is the single most important catalyst for the next wave of blockchain-based financial services. Regulatory Clarity Unlocks Institutional Use Throughout 2025, key legal milestones—including the resolution of the long-running Ripple vs. SEC case —have reduced the compliance risk that kept many institutions on the sidelines. Financial firms can now plan product rollouts and partnerships with confidence, knowing that the legal status of XRP and the XRPL network is no longer in question. This regulatory green light has transformed cautious interest into an active strategy. All evidence points to XRP and XRPL being used after the laws are effective. As Ripple has orchestrated acquisitions, licenses, expansion of trust lines on the ledger to facilitate more transactions flowing through XRP. No one knows the price it could reach, what we do know is… — VincentScott (@VincentSco72192) September 19, 2025 Strategic Acquisitions and Licensing Ripple’s recent acquisitions and pursuit of banking and payment licenses illustrate a deliberate effort to integrate XRPL into the global financial system. By securing regulatory approvals and expanding its corporate footprint, Ripple is positioning the ledger as a backbone for high-volume settlement, not merely a platform for speculative trading. These moves signal a clear intent to bridge traditional finance with tokenized, on-chain assets. XRPL’s Technical Edge The XRP Ledger is uniquely designed for institutional adoption. Its native decentralized exchange, low transaction costs, and trust-line architecture enable seamless issuance and transfer of tokenized assets, including stablecoins backed by real-world assets (RWA). We are on X, follow us to connect with us :- @TimesTabloid1 — TimesTabloid (@TimesTabloid1) June 15, 2025 Each transaction consumes a minute amount of XRP as a fee , providing a deflationary mechanism while ensuring network security and efficiency. Stablecoins and Real-World Assets Ripple’s launch of RLUSD, a U.S. dollar–pegged stablecoin, exemplifies how XRPL can serve as a settlement layer for RWA-backed digital currencies. Partnerships with top financial institutions and asset managers demonstrate the tangible potential of audited, collateralized stablecoins for seamless, instant cross-border transactions, independent of traditional banking systems. A Measured Path Forward While no one can predict XRP’s future price, the infrastructure being built points to a network whose value lies in utility rather than speculation. The combination of legal clarity, strategic acquisitions, and proven technical capacity places XRPL at the heart of the emerging tokenized financial ecosystem. As Vincent Scott suggests, the real story is not a price target but a structural shift: a global payment network ready to operate at scale once the laws are effective—and now increasingly difficult for institutions to ignore. Disclaimer : This content is meant to inform and should not be considered financial advice. The views expressed in this article may include the author’s personal opinions and do not represent Times Tabloid’s opinion. Readers are urged to do in-depth research before making any investment decisions. Any action taken by the reader is strictly at their own risk. Times Tabloid is not responsible for any financial losses. Follow us on Twitter , Facebook , Telegram , and Google News The post Journalist: All Evidence Points to XRP and XRPL Being Used After the Laws Are Effective appeared first on Times Tabloid .', 'KEYWORDS': 'Cryptocurrency|News|XRP|XRP Ledger', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758398762, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 67, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'timestabloid', 'NAME': 'TimesTabloid', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/67/default.png', 'URL': 'https://timestabloid.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422416, 'CREATED_ON': 1664381507, 'UPDATED_ON': 1673235440}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 41, 'NAME': 'REGULATION', 'CATEGORY': 'REGULATION'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 55, 'NAME': 'WALLET', 'CATEGORY': 'WALLET'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026332, 'GUID': 'https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-accelerate-world-heads-fourth-turning', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758398724, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cointelegraph.png', 'TITLE': \"Bitcoin will 'accelerate' as world heads into the Fourth Turning — Analyst\", 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Cointelegraph by Vince Quill', 'URL': 'https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-accelerate-world-heads-fourth-turning?utm_source=rss_feed&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound', 'SOURCE_ID': 16, 'BODY': 'BTC will continue to appreciate and gain adoption as the global financial and geopolitical system is reshaped in the coming decades.', 'KEYWORDS': '', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758398961, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 16, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cointelegraph', 'NAME': 'CoinTelegraph', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cointelegraph.png', 'URL': 'https://cointelegraph.com/rss', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1382227200, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 66, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422398, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711620813}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026131, 'GUID': 'https://ambcrypto.com/?p=530172', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758398434, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'TITLE': 'Bitcoin defies September slump: Mapping BTC’s path to $130K', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Evans Boto', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/bitcoin-defies-september-slump-mapping-btcs-path-to-130k/', 'SOURCE_ID': 32, 'BODY': 'Will BTC’s $123K breakout erase a decade of weak Septembers?', 'KEYWORDS': 'Bitcoin|BTC Trading View|News|News 1|Social|Trading View|ambcrypto', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758398517, 'UPDATED_ON': None, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 32, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'ambcrypto', 'NAME': 'AMB Crypto', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/ambcrypto.png', 'URL': 'https://ambcrypto.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422425, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1674467937}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026138, 'GUID': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/?p=178393', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758398420, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/52026138.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'What is “Smart Money” and How Does it Influence the Crypto Market', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Bitcoin Sistemi', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/what-is-smart-money-and-how-does-it-influence-the-crypto-market/', 'SOURCE_ID': 81, 'BODY': 'The term “smart money” is a throwback to old-school finance, where it was used pejoratively to describe lowly retail speculators while venerating the institutional investor, hedge fund or seasoned trader they take as their counterpart. The idea has also moved into the cryptocurrency space. Here, smart money means both institutions and early-stage whales who invest and use their capital thoughtfully. They are the holders who sit on their hands for prolonged periods, leave near the top of a parabola and frequently control liquidity flows across exchanges. That’s because retail traders move in response to headlines and feelings, while smart money trades on research (and connections) — as well as conviction over the longer term. For novice investors, tracking where this capital is going can be as valuable as studying charts. More and more projects drawing in smart money early are the ones that fill headlines months later. MAGACOIN FINANCE has simply proven to be one of them. How smart money moves Smart money in crypto is often identified through on-chain analytics. Because blockchain transactions are transparent, anyone can observe large transfers and wallet activity. Sophisticated investors use platforms like Nansen, Glassnode, and Santiment to detect accumulation patterns and liquidity shifts before they play out in the broader market. For instance, a cluster of whale wallets steadily buying a token without selling often signals underlying conviction. Conversely, rapid inflows to exchanges from known whale wallets can warn of impending sell pressure. In 2025, these patterns show smart money diversifying beyond Bitcoin and Ethereum into Layer-1 projects, DeFi protocols, and carefully structured presales. Analysts note that the most successful traders aren’t necessarily trying to outsmart whales but to ride the same wave once the signals become clear. Influence on price cycle s Smart money does not simply trade in markets; it makes markets. Capital concentration leads the sentiment of liquidity, and when the whales join in advance, it creates an environment that retail later adds to. This reflexive loop has characterized almost every major crypto cycle. Bitcoin´s parabolic moves went into overdrive when institutions entered the market; Ethereum´s growth was secured when money started flowing to DeFi protocols. Today, the same process is taking place with meme coins and presales. Analysts say that in any sustained bull run, once smart money indicates fulfillment (you will know when buy signals are definitive), the crowd plays catch-up, and prices move exponentially. But those cycles are rare in stocks, where information advantages and private deals often obscure outcomes. Crypto’s open ledgers mean that smart-money behavior is visible, and retail investors have a rare opportunity to join the ranks of informed capital before stories become popular. The excitement surrounding MAGACOIN FINANCE stems not only from the presale raise but also from the potential upside. If adoption takes place in line with forecasts, a $2,000 stake could feasibly balloon to $40,000—a 20x return in the most cautious scenarios, with upside potential far beyond that. Throwing gas on the fire is a bonus code PATRIOT50X, which provides early buyers with 50% more tokens prior to listings. Analysts say that structured incentives like these are what propelled BONK and WIF, which built an unstoppable demand for both through retail stacking allocations that whales could not refuse. Feast-or-famine design: You make these supply-side-based systems, and you get more demand as supplies become tighter, Smith explains in this video about his proposal. To these investors, missing out on this opportunity could mean missing out on generational returns, as the project shifts from niche awareness to mainstream buzz. Why retail watches smart money Retail investors may not have the resources of institutions, but they can observe where smart money is flowing. Tracking wallet activity, monitoring exchange inflows, and studying presale participation all reveal valuable clues. When whale wallets show accumulation in projects with strong tokenomics, it often signals a bullish setup. Retail then rides the wave, compounding the impact of early positioning. This reflexive loop, where smart money signals attract retail, and retail amplifies the trend, is what fuels many of crypto’s largest rallies. Analysts caution that blindly following whales carries risks, but when combined with research, it becomes one of the most effective strategies for spotting momentum early. In this way, smart money acts as both a compass and a catalyst, guiding the market while accelerating trends once retail catches on. Lessons from past cycl es History shows the fingerprints of smart money in every breakout. Bitcoin’s institutional adoption in 2020 turned a quiet bull run into a global rally. Ethereum’s DeFi summer in 2021 was sparked by whale accumulation in governance tokens months before retail noticed. Even meme coins like Dogecoin and Shiba Inu gained unstoppable momentum after whales began stacking positions, signaling conviction that retail later validated. Analysts argue that these precedents are what make current presales so closely watched. When smart money participates early, retail sees it as confirmation that the narrative has legs. This pattern is repeating with MAGACOIN FINANCE, where presale growth and structured incentives are already being tracked by on-chain analysts as a sign of broader adoption to come. Conclusion: smart money and the new cyc le The direction of crypto markets will always be influenced by smart money, but how far narratives go is decided by retail. From Bitcoin’s early institutional inflows to today’s altcoin rotations, the message remains clear: follow where informed capital is moving. Now with a 20x growth forecast and the PATRIOT50X bonus code promoting adoption, MAGACOIN FINANCE is shining light on a project combining smart money conviction with retail enthusiasm. Analysts say this sort of matching, of whale conviction with community size, paves the way for outsize moves. As new cycles play out, the winners will probably be the ones who got in first, held through volatility, and realized that smart money isn’t just a sign of momentum but a galvanizing force behind it. To learn more about MAGACOIN FINANCE, visit: Website: https://magacoinfinance.com Access: https://magacoinfinance.com/access Twitter/X: https://x.com/magacoinfinance Telegram: https://t.me/magacoinfinance Continue Reading: What is “Smart Money” and How Does it Influence the Crypto Market', 'KEYWORDS': 'Sponsored', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758398524, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758398526, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 81, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinsistemi', 'NAME': 'BitcoinSistemi', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/81/default.png', 'URL': 'https://en.bitcoinsistemi.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422423, 'CREATED_ON': 1692873798, 'UPDATED_ON': 1692873836}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 62, 'NAME': 'ZRX', 'CATEGORY': 'ZRX'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026106, 'GUID': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/?p=824832', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758398415, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/21/52026106.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Litecoin Price Compresses In Tight Falling Wedge, Breakout Ahead?', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Godspower Owie', 'URL': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/news/litecoin/litecoin-show-hidden-strength/', 'SOURCE_ID': 21, 'BODY': 'In his latest update, CryptoWzrd observed that Litecoin closed the day on a bearish note, moving in line with Bitcoin’s broader trend. He stressed that the LTC/BTC chart remains within a falling wedge formation. CryptoWzrd added that he will be keeping a close watch on the intraday action over the weekend to scout for quick scalp opportunities, particularly if Bitcoin lends further confirmation to the setup. Falling Wedge Formation Holds The Key CryptoWzrd highlighted that both Litecoin’s daily chart and the LTC/BTC pair closed on a bearish note. Despite this short-term weakness, he pointed out that LTC/BTC continues to maintain a falling wedge formation, a structure that historically favors bullish reversals when broken to the upside. Related Reading: Litecoin Clings To Ascending Trendline As Bulls Eye $135 Breakout He explained that a healthy breakout from this wedge could trigger a strong upside rally, with Litecoin likely to follow suit and reflect the broader market sentiment. Such a move would mark a significant shift in momentum, particularly after the recent bearish closes, and could attract renewed buying pressure into the market. CryptoWzrd noted that Litecoin, although trading bearish, is still holding firmly above the $112 level. He emphasized that this zone is crucial, as a single strong bullish daily candle from this area could serve as confirmation for buyers and set the stage for the next leg higher. Looking ahead, he identified $140 as the next key resistance target, a level that would need to be overcome for Litecoin to confirm a sustained rally. Should the price manage to close above $140, CryptoWzrd believes the altcoin could extend gains toward $170 and potentially open the door for a broader bullish continuation. Litecoin Intraday Volatility Picks Up Conclusively, the analyst noted that Litecoin’s intraday chart showed noticeable volatility today, a sign that price movements could remain sharp in the near term. He suggested that traders should anticipate more swings from this location, as the market attempts to establish a clearer direction. Related Reading: Litecoin Is On Fire: $120–$125 Range In Bullish Crosshairs The expert emphasized that for Litecoin to shift into a more positive stance, it must hold above the $115.50 intraday resistance. A successful move above this level could provide the momentum needed to push higher, with $123 standing out as the next resistance target on the upside. For now, his focus remains on lower time frame charts to identify quick scalp opportunities. Given that trading conditions tend to be thinner and less predictable over the weekend, he added that his expectations will remain measured, preferring to wait for a healthy setup before committing to new positions. Featured image from Adobe Stock, chart from Tradingview.com', 'KEYWORDS': 'Litecoin|bitcoin|CryptoWzrd|Litecoin news|litecoin price|ltc|LTC news|ltc price|ltc/usd|ltcbtc|LTCUSDT', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758398500, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758398500, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 21, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'newsbtc', 'NAME': 'NewsBTC', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/newsbtc.png', 'URL': 'https://www.newsbtc.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1380585600, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 50, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422399, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1711620962}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 50, 'NAME': 'TRADING', 'CATEGORY': 'TRADING'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 33, 'NAME': 'LTC', 'CATEGORY': 'LTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 14, 'NAME': 'BTC', 'CATEGORY': 'BTC'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 37, 'NAME': 'MARKET', 'CATEGORY': 'MARKET'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52026111, 'GUID': '585674', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758398408, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/13/52026111.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'US Treasury Seeks Public Comment On Implementation Of GENIUS Act – Details', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Opeyemi Sule', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinist.com/us-treasury-seeks-public-comment-genius-stablecoin/', 'SOURCE_ID': 13, 'BODY': 'The United States Treasury Department has opened a request for public comment on the implementation of the Guiding and Establishing National Innovation for US Stablecoins (GENIUS) Act. The GENIUS Act, signed into US law in July, was designed to provide a regulatory framework for stablecoin issuers. This latest call for public input comes exactly a month after the Request for Comment on Innovative Methods to Detect Illicit Activity linked to payment stablecoins. At the time, the US Treasury was interested in gathering feedback on different technologies to identify and combat the risks associated with these dollar-backed digital assets. Call For Public Comment On Stablecoin Act To Close In 30 Days On Thursday, September 18, the US Department of the Treasury issued an Advance Notice of Proposed Rulemaking (ANPRM), calling on the public for comments on the implementation of the GENIUS Act. This request will allow a wide range of stakeholders to contribute, by offering data and other information, to the implementation of this law. The press release read: The GENIUS Act tasks the Treasury with issuing regulations that encourage innovation in payment stablecoins while also providing an appropriately tailored regime to protect consumers, mitigate potential illicit finance risks, and address financial stability risks. This notice asked for comments and views on a plethora of questions, including whether extra clarity is needed on the amount of reserve assets required to be held in custody. “Are there foreign payment stablecoin regulatory or supervisory regimes, or regimes in development, that may be comparable to the regime established under the GENIUS Act?” another question posed. Some of the other questions asked in this notice include marketing restrictions, balancing state-level and federal oversight, and the application of Bank Secrecy Act (BSA), anti-money laundering regulations, and sanctions obligations. The Treasury Department noted that the public should submit their comments in response to the ANPRM within 30 days of publication in the Federal Register. Crypto Market Structure Bill To Undergo Vote In September Indeed, signing the GENIUS Act into law represented a major breakthrough in regulating the crypto landscape in the United States. In its next move, the US Senate is looking to hold a vote on the crypto market structure bill, titled the Responsible Financial Innovation Act 2025, before the end of September. The digital market structure bill is aimed at clarifying the roles of various financial agencies in the oversight and enforcement of crypto regulations. In an updated version, the Senate Banking Committee addressed the issue of blockchain developers being treated as financial institutions and non-fungible tokens (NFTs) being treated as securities.', 'KEYWORDS': 'Stablecoin|crypto|GENIUS Act|stablecoin|US Senate|US Treasury', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758398503, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758398503, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 13, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitcoinist', 'NAME': 'Bitcoinist', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/bitcoinist.png', 'URL': 'https://bitcoinist.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUN