s not produced the kind of presale multipliers that early-stage investors crave. XRP Tundra offers that contrast. Its presale delivers TUNDRA-S, a utility and yield token issued on Solana, while also granting free TUNDRA-X on the XRP Ledger, a governance and reserve asset. In the first presale phase, TUNDRA-S is fixed at $0.01, accompanied by a 19% bonus. Each purchase includes free TUNDRA-X valued at $0.005, effectively doubling early exposure. At launch, the targets are $2.50 for TUNDRA-S and $1.25 for TUNDRA-X, outlining a 2500% return potential. For Near investors accustomed to gradual network growth, that kind of presale design appears transformative. Staking Tools That XRP Never Had One reason Near supporters are paying attention is XRP Tundra’s solution for staking, an area long absent from Ripple’s ecosystem. Through Cryo Vaults, participants will be able to lock XRP for 7, 30, 60, or 90 days, earning up to 30% APY. The system keeps assets entirely on-ledger, reducing custodial risk. Frost Keys, NFT-based boosters, allow participants to increase multipliers or shorten lockups, creating flexibility without sacrificing control. While staking is not yet live, presale buyers will be first in line to activate the system. The balance of predictable yield and user control has resonated with Near investors who prioritize utility alongside growth. Verified Trust Through Multiple Audits Unlike many presales that ask for blind faith, XRP Tundra has invested in third-party verification. Independent contract reviews are available from Cyberscope , Solidproof , and Freshcoins . Each report strengthens confidence that the project is technically sound. The team has also completed KYC verification with Vital Block , offering transparency uncommon in early-stage launches. In addition, community content has begun amplifying the project. For example, Crypto Volt recently highlighted the presale’s mechanics and its implications for long-term holders. Why Near Investors Call It a “Golden Ticket” For Near Protocol investors, XRP Tundra is seen as an opportunity to enter at the ground floor of a dual-token system with audited security, NFT-enhanced staking, and the potential for 2500% returns. While Ripple’s ecosystem continues to evolve and Near develops its infrastructure, XRP Tundra is commanding attention by offering something tangible today: a presale economy that blends transparency with transformative upside. For those looking beyond technical milestones to financial breakthroughs, this may be the ticket worth holding. Follow XRP Tundra’s presale and community updates: Website: https://www.xrptundra.com/ Medium: https://medium.com/@xrptundra Telegram: https://t.me/xrptundra X: https://x.com/Xrptundra Contact: Tim Fénix, contact@xrptundra.com Disclaimer: This is a sponsored article and is for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Crypto Daily, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice.', 'KEYWORDS': 'More News', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758409672, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758409673, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 75, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptodaily', 'NAME': 'Crypto Daily', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/75/default.png', 'URL': 'https://cryptodaily.co.uk/feed', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422419, 'CREATED_ON': 1685543991, 'UPDATED_ON': 1685544026}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 89, 'NAME': 'NEAR', 'CATEGORY': 'NEAR'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52031588, 'GUID': 'https://bitzo.com/2025/09/exploring-the-unique-opportunities-of-xrp-tundra-for-near-protocol-investors', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758395915, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/104/52031588.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Exploring the Unique Opportunities of XRP Tundra for Near Protocol Investors', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Bitzo', 'URL': 'https://bitzo.com/2025/09/exploring-the-unique-opportunities-of-xrp-tundra-for-near-protocol-investors', 'SOURCE_ID': 104, 'BODY': \"As the blockchain space evolves, Near Protocol investors have consistently sought platforms that not only provide robust technology but also offer substantial financial growth opportunities. This pursuit has recently directed their attention towards XRP Tundra, a project that bridges the benefits of the XRP Ledger with the technological prowess of Solana. With a presale price of merely $0.01, XRP Tundra has been introduced to the market, aiming for a future value of $2.50 for its utility token and $1.25 for its governance token. This substantial growth potential is stirring discussions among investors, often referred to as the “golden ticket effect”. A Closer Look at XRP Tundra’s Dual-Token Model XRP Tundra distinguishes itself with an intriguing dual-token system. During its initial presale phase, buyers gain access to TUNDRA-S, the project's main utility token at a locked price of $0.01, alongside a 19% purchase bonus. This phase also features TUNDRA-X tokens, offered at $0.005 each, enhancing investor portfolios by doubling their token holdings early in the project’s lifecycle. The dual-token model is structured to maximize investor returns and govern the ecosystem effectively. The diagram below provides a visual insight into how these tokens interact within the ecosystem. Enhanced Staking Capabilities Unlike XRP’s previous limitations in staking, XRP Tundra introduces Cryo Vaults which offer up to 30% APY for staking durations as brief as 7 days, and up to 90 days. This approach not only secures assets on-ledger but also integrates NFT-based Frost Keys to encourage flexible staking strategies without compromising security or asset control. Here’s another key visual that demonstrates the expected performance and benefits of engaging with XRP Tundra’s innovative staking solutions. Ensuring Investor Confidence Through Audits and KYC To solidify trust, XRP Tundra has undergone rigorous audits from reputable third-party services such as Cyberscope , Solidproof , and Freshcoins . Moreover, the project has completed KYC verification with Vital Block , enhancing its credibility and transparency. For those keen on exploring further, details about XRP Tundra, its roadmap, and investment opportunities can be accessed through their official website , or by following their updates on Medium , Telegram , and X . For direct inquiries, potential investors can reach out to Tim Fénix at contact@xrptundra.com . Disclaimer: This is a sponsored article and is for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Bitzo, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice.\", 'KEYWORDS': 'More News|Altcoins', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'POSITIVE', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758409917, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758409917, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 104, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'bitzo', 'NAME': 'Bitzo', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/104/default.png', 'URL': 'https://bitzo.com/feed', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': 1520899200, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422434, 'CREATED_ON': 1736502919, 'UPDATED_ON': 1736502976}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 58, 'NAME': 'XRP', 'CATEGORY': 'XRP'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 89, 'NAME': 'NEAR', 'CATEGORY': 'NEAR'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 13, 'NAME': 'BLOCKCHAIN', 'CATEGORY': 'BLOCKCHAIN'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52025366, 'GUID': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/?p=814134', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758395770, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/43/52025366.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Helius Labs CEO and Solana co-founder Anatoly publicly disagreed over tokenization', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': 'Hannah Collymore', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/helius-labs-ceo-solana-co-founder-disagree/', 'SOURCE_ID': 43, 'BODY': \"Helius Labs CEO Mert Mumtaz and one of Solana’s co-founders, Anatoly “Toly” Yakovenko, publicly aired differing opinions on X around the polarizing topic of tokenization. The Solana camp has always been close-knit and closely bonded by a shared underdog mentality, callused by challenges like downtimes after it burst onto the scene as the “Ethereum Killer.” So, when major parties have a clash of ideals, it tends to get noticed. Why create a token? The exchange between Toly and Mert began after the Solana co-founder responded to a post by the latter asking why a wallet needs a token. “Is there some use for it that I’m missing?” He asked, to which Toly wrote , “Everything with revenues should have a token.” Pushing for an explanation, Mert asked, “Why?” and Toly says, “So then the profits could be returned to token holders.” In the comment section, users were also divided. While some acknowledged the logic in Toly’s position, others leaned towards Mert’s view that wallets are essential infrastructure that risk becoming something else when tokenization is involved. Toly’s response seems to be more about democratizing ownership than anything else, and it paves the way for regular users to benefit as opposed to just VCs or a centralized team. Mert seemed to disagree as he replied with a sarcastic “should I release token?” The exchange is only an example of the debates about tokenization going on all over the ecosystem as the space further matures. Just days earlier, Mert ignited a round of debate after floating the idea of a Solana-aligned stablecoin in a conversation about tokenized treasuries and stablecoins, which is an easy way to capture yield on-chain. Mert stirred debate on Solana stablecoins On September 10, Mert floated the idea of a Solana-aligned stablecoin whose reserve yield would be redirected to SOL via buybacks or burns—either as an “enshrined” protocol feature or, more likely, via competing digital-asset treasury companies (DATs). “Warming up to the idea that Solana should enshrine a stablecoin,” he wrote, adding that “50% burn of the yield goes back to burning SOL.” Hours later, he reiterated: “It shouldn’t be enshrined, a DAT should do it… fix it and trillions.” Mumtaz’s core critique focuses on what he describes as “yield leakage” from Solana. “Stablecoins are commodities, and currently on Solana, there is one that captures all yield and literally funds Solana’s biggest competitor with it!” As far as he is concerned, under the US GENIUS Act , stables are readily swappable and issuers will compete aggressively for market share—something that is already being seen with the recent “Bachelor-style” scramble among large stablecoin companies to court business. “If you don’t want to enshrine a Solana-centric stable, then consider digital asset treasury companies (DATs)… The DAT is literally a machine for buying the underlying token.” That framing clashes with the GENIUS Act, which carves out “payment stablecoins” as neither securities nor commodities for US federal purposes, consolidating oversight largely under banking regulators and expressly separating them from SEC/CFTC jurisdiction. Since stablecoins cannot pass interest to holders, issuers (or affiliated structures) capture the reserve income and can decide how to use it, and this is the lever Mumtaz wants pointed back at Solana . Don’t just read crypto news. Understand it. Subscribe to our newsletter. It's free .\", 'KEYWORDS': 'News|SOL', 'LANG': 'EN', 'UPVOTES': 0, 'DOWNVOTES': 0, 'SCORE': 0, 'SENTIMENT': 'NEUTRAL', 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'CREATED_ON': 1758396901, 'UPDATED_ON': 1758413325, 'SOURCE_DATA': {'TYPE': '120', 'ID': 43, 'SOURCE_KEY': 'cryptopolitan', 'NAME': 'Cryptopolitan', 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://images.cryptocompare.com/news/default/cryptopolitan.png', 'URL': 'https://www.cryptopolitan.com/feed/', 'LANG': 'EN', 'SOURCE_TYPE': 'RSS', 'LAUNCH_DATE': None, 'SORT_ORDER': 0, 'BENCHMARK_SCORE': 0, 'STATUS': 'ACTIVE', 'LAST_UPDATED_TS': 1758422422, 'CREATED_ON': 1657730129, 'UPDATED_ON': 1681205909}, 'CATEGORY_DATA': [{'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 211, 'NAME': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY', 'CATEGORY': 'CRYPTOCURRENCY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 46, 'NAME': 'SOL', 'CATEGORY': 'SOL'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 209, 'NAME': 'DIGITAL ASSET TREASURY', 'CATEGORY': 'DIGITAL ASSET TREASURY'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 25, 'NAME': 'EXCHANGE', 'CATEGORY': 'EXCHANGE'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 26, 'NAME': 'FIAT', 'CATEGORY': 'FIAT'}, {'TYPE': '122', 'ID': 15, 'NAME': 'BUSINESS', 'CATEGORY': 'BUSINESS'}]}, {'TYPE': '121', 'ID': 52024892, 'GUID': 'https://seekingalpha.com/news/4496784-key-deals-this-week-brighthouse-financial-workday-paramount-skydance-radian-group-roche-and-more?utm_source=cryptocompare.com&utm_medium=referral&feed_item_type=news', 'PUBLISHED_ON': 1758395739, 'PUBLISHED_ON_NS': None, 'IMAGE_URL': 'https://resources.cryptocompare.com/news/50/52024892.jpeg', 'TITLE': 'Key deals this week: Brighthouse Financial, Workday, Paramount Skydance, Radian Group, Roche and more', 'SUBTITLE': None, 'AUTHORS': '', 'URL': 'https://seekingalpha.com/news/4496784-key-deals-this-week-brighthouse-financial-workday-paramount-skydance-radian-group-roche-and-more?utm_source=cryptocompare.com&utm_medium=referral&feed_item_type=news', 'SOURCE_ID': 50, 'BODY': \"More on M&A tickers, etc. Rithm Capital And Paramount: Ascendant Asset Manager Enters Booming Manhattan Office Real Estate Brighthouse: Acquisition Appears Likely Invest Smar